From 70270893b4340ffddbcf95e69a459f7135164746 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:29:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] update check: a test build (alpha) looks for and offers no
 update

A build stamped _ALPHA is a test build of the unified tree, published from
the lean branch Dev-Uni and installed by hand. It must never be offered
another image: the stable line is older, and a Dev beta would take the
router off the tree it is testing.

- reaper_webs_update.sh ends before the manifest is fetched when EXTENDNO
  carries _ALPHA, and reports webs_state_channel=alpha. The scheduled check
  and an AiMesh-triggered one end there too.
- Firmware page: says why in place of "up to date" (RFWU_62, 25 packs), an
  ALPHA badge beside the installed version, and the node comparison knows
  an alpha build from a beta of the same number.

No effect on a stable or beta build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../router/rom/webs_scripts/reaper_webs_update.sh  | 14 ++++++++++++++
 release/src/router/www/BR.dict                     |  1 +
